(defparameter fib_array (list 0 1)) ; fib_array = (0 1)
(defun sums (N)
    (cond 
        ((null N) 0) ; if null, return 0 
        ((< N 0) 0) ; if negative, return 0
        ((< N (length fib_array)) 0) ; if it is already in array, return 0
        (t (+ 1 ; count this addition
                (sums (- N 1)) ; add additions from fib(N-1)
                (sums (- N 2)) ; add additions from fib(N-2)
        ))
    )
)

|#
Answer to question: computing fib(n) requires computing fib(n-1) and fib(n-2), and each of those require their own additions. 
sums almost mirrors fib(N) except that it has one more for it accounts for the addition being performed at the current level.
